            <ArticleTitle>Intra-operative and short term outcome of total knee arthroplasty in morbidly obese patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>784-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.knee.2014.02.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0968-0160(14)00043-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Longer operation times, poorer patient outcomes and increased early post-operative complications are reasons cited for not undertaking total knee arthroplasty (TKA) on morbidly obese patients. This study tests the hypothesis that there is no difference in intra-operative parameters between morbidly obese and non-obese patients, and no difference in patient outcome.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Intra-operative parameters, post-operative complications, patient outcomes and knee range of motion were compared between morbidly obese patients (BMI&gt;40 kg/m2) and individually age and gender matched non-obese patients (BMI&lt;30 kg/m2) undergoing cementless rotating platform TKA.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Anaesthetic times and length of hospital stay were not significantly different between the morbidly obese and non-obese patients. Surgical time was significantly greater in morbidly obese patients. Improvements in patient outcomes following TKA were not significantly different between the morbidly obese and non-obese patients at early and short-term follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">In contrast to previous studies, post-operative complication rates within three months of surgery and up to one year post-operatively were not significantly higher for morbidly obese patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LEVEL OF EVIDENCE" NlmCategory="METHODS">III.</AbstractText>
